 "notes": "95% CL upper limit on dark photon kinetic mixing epsilon from Fig. 3 (e-print file constraints_newrange_ellmin2_withbias_nodrop.png), digitized programmatically from the raster figure (red 'Joint' curve, the combined unWISE Blue + Green x Planck NILC dark-screening cross-correlation, which the paper presents as its main result; radio-bias-subtracted data). Axis calibration from major tick/gridline pixel positions. Curve traced from m_A' = 1.5e-13 eV (start of the paper's mass scan) to ~5.7e-12 eV where the curve exits the top of the plot (epsilon = 1e-5); the scan formally extends to 9.7e-12 eV but the limit is weaker than 1e-5 there. Minimum epsilon ~ 3.9e-8 near 4e-13 eV, consistent with the quoted epsilon < 4e-8. No dark-matter density assumption: signal is conversion of CMB photons in large-scale structure, independent of DP relic abundance.",
